{"The current logic for determining committable offsets uses a range loop from last committed to maximum seen offset, which will stall offset commits indefinitely if there are gaps in offsets received (due to Kafka control messages, compaction, or filtering). Should iterate over sorted set of actually recorded offsets instead.": 0.8784628510475159, "queue.ShutDown exception and queue.Queue.shutdown method were introduced in Python 3.13, causing AttributeError or NameError in older Python versions (e.g., 3.11). Worker threads blocked on work_queue.get() will not exit gracefully when shutdown is set to True.": 0.9453127384185791, "q.shutdown is not available in Python versions prior to 3.13. Should use sentinel values (e.g., None) to signal shutdown to workers instead.": 0.9495635628700256, "Starting a new Sentry transaction for every single message in a high-throughput consumer is extremely expensive and can lead to performance degradation or rate-limiting. Including worker_id in transaction name creates high cardinality. Should use sentry_sdk.start_span instead or wrap larger batches in single transaction.": 0.7793741226196289, "The message field in the WorkItem dataclass appears to be unused throughout the worker and tracker logic, causing unnecessary memory overhead per queued item.": 0.26630452275276184}